Gateway system, firmware and WAN-health reads
===========================================

OPNsense system identity/time and firmware product fields follow pinned upstream
contracts. Localized version/update strings are not parsed as structured data.
Unobserved system resources remain absent. Firmware errors are unavailable;
unchecked update state is unknown, and a missing latest version is not replaced
with the installed version. Repository/mirror subscription data is not exposed.

Live monitor rows require successful status, unique names and complete routing
search metadata. The latter also contains disabled or inactive gateways, so its
row count need not equal the live-monitor row count. Live rows must have a unique
configuration match. Default-route flags come from the active routing search.
Machine states control health labels. Raw none with numeric monitor samples means
no active alarm; raw none without samples is unmonitored. Missing samples remain
unknown and measured zero stays zero. Invalid samples are unavailable.

The normalized service boundary validates complete firmware/health envelopes and
returns generic 501 for declared unsupported reads and 502 for unavailable data.
Cancellation propagates. Firmware reads recheck scope and contact the adapter on
every request; packages/plugins keep their existing scoped cache policy. The UI
validates selected-gateway identity, suppresses stale read data, offers retries
and distinguishes loading, empty, unavailable and unknown. Sync metadata remains
visible independently of live firmware status.

These changes introduce no gateway writes. Synthetic transport, identity and
browser fixtures are not installed-firmware acceptance or normal production
login on a physical gateway. Other vendor schemas, mutations, operational health,
managed backup storage/retention/restore, sustained operation and enterprise
recovery/support objectives require separate evidence. A successful scan or
finite qualification run is not an enterprise certification.
